//? Title: Eratosthenes: actual crossing stages
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Listing all primes up to an inclusive bound requires removing composites without
repeating a separate primality proof for every integer. The sieve crosses
multiples of surviving primes starting at their squares. We expose the actual
strikes up to30 and retain the prime-counting comparisons through10000.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

A composite m has a prime factor p no greater than its square root; otherwise
both factors would exceed the square root. When the scan reaches p, every
smaller multiple p*k with k<p already has a smaller prime factor. Therefore
crossings start at p squared and only primes with p<=n/p are needed.

$$ \sum_{p\leq\sqrt n}\left(\left\lfloor\frac np\right\rfloor-p+1\right)=O(n\log\log n).$$
\alttext(The number of strike assignments is the sum over crossing primes of floor n divided by p minus p plus one, with order n log log n growth.)

An already false bit is still an actual strike assignment and counts again.
Newly composite counts include only true-to-false transitions. The bit mask uses
linear storage; optional captured strikes add work-sized storage. Prime-counting
approximations n/log n are asymptotic references, not exact bounds at the
displayed small values.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/sieve_of_eratosthenes_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/random/quality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/sieve_of_eratosthenes.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::prime_sieve_trace(10);
    std::print("| crossing prime | actual strikes | newly composite |\n| ---: | --- | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.stages)
        std::print("| {} | `{}` | {} |\n", s.prime, s.strikes, s.newly_composite);
    std::print("\nPrimes: `{}`.\n", r.primes);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Integers 2 through 10");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual strikes", r.strikes));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0}, std::format("Survivors {}", r.primes));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/sieve_of_eratosthenes_tiny.svg");
}
```
