> API and interpretation

For compatibility the mask is empty below2, otherwise has n+1 bits. Allocation
geometry and n+1 overflow are checked; loops use division and guarded increment
rather than overflowing p*p or m+p conditions. Default n bound is100million.
Limits are input/mark/record policies, not peak memory estimates. This
controlled number-theory calculation needs no real dataset.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- Hardy and Wright, An Introduction to the Theory of Numbers,6th edition,2008

